  "worked_solution": "The correct answer is the following. \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13945275/assets/441277a2f5c960a02d84707d21746da558e136168dc951a931f5354abf4a283e.png)\n\nIndeed, we have that $g(x)$ is continuous on the open interval $(-4,1).$\n\nNotice that:\n\n- $f(x)$ is not continuous at $x=0,$ but this point lies within the interval $(-4,1),$\n\n- $p(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-3,$ but this point lies within the interval $(-4,1),$\n\n- $h(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-2,$ but this point lies within the interval $(-4,1),$\n\n- $q(x)$ is not continuous at $x=-1,$ but this point lies within the interval $(-4,1).$",
